# Container crontab (supercronic) — times are ET; the image sets TZ=America/New_York.
# The Mac crontab.txt ran these at 12:30/12:40/12:56 PT = 3:30/3:40/3:56 ET.
# Output goes to stdout → Railway logs (no file redirects).
# MLB Top Picks maintenance (that service has no scheduler of its own; this
# reaches it over Railway's private network). 10:00 ET grades yesterday's
# picks; 11:00/13:00 refresh today's as real lineup cards replace projections.
0 10,11,13 * * * curl -sS --max-time 120 http://mlb.railway.internal:3000/mlb-matchups/api/picks/cron
# Intraday profit-take sweep, every 30 min from 9:30 ET to 3:00 ET. Catches
# an option that doubles at 11am and fades before the close passes run.
# Silent (no log spam, no alert) unless something actually fires.
30 9-14 * * 1-5 python /app/paper_trader.py --profit-take
0 10-15 * * 1-5 python /app/paper_trader.py --profit-take
30 15 * * 1-5 python /app/engulfing_scanner.py
40 15 * * 1-5 python /app/paper_trader.py
# First chase (3:48 ET): give the 3:40 option entries a shot at a marketable
# fill before the spot-check wave adds more orders.
48 15 * * 1-5 python /app/paper_trader.py --chase
# Spot check (3:50 ET): re-scan, record anything new, alert ONLY on deltas —
# new signals or earlier ones that no longer hold (SPCX 2026-08-03: spiked
# 3:45 ET, 15 min after the main scan, and was never seen).
50 15 * * 1-5 python /app/engulfing_scanner.py --delta
# Second entry pass (3:52 ET): trade anything the spot check just surfaced
# (entries are per-leg idempotent — signals already traded are untouched).
52 15 * * 1-5 python /app/paper_trader.py
56 15 * * 1-5 python /app/paper_trader.py --chase
# Close verdict (4:05 ET): the engulfing pattern is a DAILY-CLOSE pattern, so
# the final word — including a close that engulfs in the last seconds — is
# only knowable after 4:00. Delta-alerts like the spot check; quiet if the
# 3:30/3:50 picture held.
5 16 * * 1-5 python /app/engulfing_scanner.py --delta --at-close
